  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-02T21:05:39.078Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Provide an optional VRC_IKController component that can be attached to avatars. This component would expose the IK weight sliders for the arms, legs, head, and torso in the FinalIK controller as well as a toggle for switching between a head-based pivot and a root-based pivot for the avatar.\n\nThis would allow Mecanim animations to decide if they want the IK controllers for these joints to be enabled, disabled, or interpolated. For example: emotes such as waving, pointing, and clapping would benefit from having head IK enabled, but other ones such as backflipping or dancing would be better with it disabled. Similarly, standard walking animations benefit from foot IK and head-based pivot, but if the avatar uses a levitation animation for movement, then it would be better off with foot IK disabled and using a root-based pivot.\n\n[AvatarOverhaul]",
